For your Python AI Weather Agent, you can implement semantic caching using Redis Stack or Redis with vector search. This lets your application reuse an earlier answer when a new query has a similar meaning, without calling CrewAI and the LLM every time.

Since your project already uses Redis, the cleanest approach is to add a semantic cache service alongside your existing Redis cache.

## 1. Architecture

FastAPI Weather Endpoint

Validate query and identify intent

Create embedding

OpenAI `text-embedding-3-small`

Redis vector search

Find similar queries and check freshness

Cache hit

Return cached response

Cache miss

Call weather tools and agent

After a successful miss, store the response and embedding with an expiration time.

One important distinction: ordinary Redis `GET`/`SET` is enough for exact caching, but semantic search requires vector search capabilities, such as Redis Search with vector indexes. If your Redis deployment does not support vector search, you can use a separate vector store or add a compatible Redis deployment.

## 2. Start Redis with vector search support

For local development, use Redis Stack, which includes Redis Search capabilities.&#x20;


